  "reason": "The current best (config_040, 0.725) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted. All tested scvi_n200 multiprofile variants are at or below this level, so further exploitation of that encoder family has diminishing returns. The largest untested variable is the RNA encoder: pca_n2000 has never been evaluated in the multiprofile multimodal setting. Config_004 pairs pca_n2000 with the proven-best downstream architecture (imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted), directly testing whether a simpler linear encoder can approach scvi_n200's performance. This is the highest-information experiment: if pca_n2000 reaches ~0.70+, it offers a cheaper alternative (expected ~2.5–3.0 GPU hours vs. 3.60 for scvi_n200), and the remaining experiment could explore further pca_n2000 variants; if it falls well below, it confirms scvi_n200 is essential and locks in config_040 as the final answer. Expected relative cost: moderate-to-low (~2.5–3.0 GPU hours), cheaper than the current best due to the simpler PCA encoder."
}

